e8s|v|To give utterance to expression of grief, pain, censure, regret. etc.; to lament; to murmur; to find fault; -- commonly used with of. Also, to creak or squeak, as a timber or wheel. ; To make a formal accusation; to make a charge. ; To lament; to bewail.	s:1hgk,68,4~1hgk,68,4
e98|n|Filled up; with no part or element lacking; free from deficiency; entire; perfect; consummate. ; Finished; ended; concluded; completed; as, the edifice is complete. ; Having all the parts or organs which belong to it or to the typical form; having calyx, corolla, stamens, and pistil.	N:16dy,44,2;1tuh,11,1~16dy,44,2;1tuh,11,1
